-Subject: [PATCH] Only mount a video's glass controls while it's near the
- viewport
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Each video's play/mute/fullscreen bar is three GlassSurface
-(backdrop-filter) elements, and the site caps simultaneous glass
-surfaces at four because backdrop-filter is expensive to composite.
-The bar was mounting as soon as a video had ever been near the
-viewport and staying mounted for good, so a page with eight videos
-(e.g. /work/reel) could hold 20+ glass surfaces at once, blowing
-through that budget on every scroll frame — the dominant remaining
-cause of the scroll jank on video-heavy pages. Gate it behind
-`active` instead, the same flag that already governs decoding, so
-only videos actually near the viewport claim a glass slot.
-
-Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxB4PXbbyDtVBArjRyHo21
