-Subject: [PATCH] Only decode video near the viewport
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-A grid page can carry a dozen autoplaying videos, and mobile browsers
-cap how many can decode at once — iOS Safari's hardware decoder tops
-out around 4-6 depending on the device — so the ones past that limit
-silently never play. Only videos within 300px of the viewport now
-carry a <source>; the rest sit on their poster frame until scrolled
-near, and drop back to it once scrolled well past, freeing the
-decoder for whichever one the viewer is at. A video the viewer
-paused on purpose stays paused when it scrolls back into range
-instead of resuming on its own.
