-From 68971439be637a49c2a68c071efd4e07f2261fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:22:48 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] Round the corners on photos and video, matching the navbar
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Every content photo and video now carries rounded-glass-lg — the same
-28px continuous corner as the header pill — instead of the site's
-previous square-cornered rule for media. The one deliberate exception
-is a full-bleed background: the videoFullscreen hero variant stays
-square, since it's the page's backdrop rather than content on its
-own. A video keeps its rounding right up until it goes fullscreen,
-where it squares off automatically (a rounded corner on a
-screen-filling video reads as a border, not a shape choice).
-
-Touches: the gallery grid and lightbox, the pair/beforeAfter/videoLoop
-and default media-block variants, project and team member photos, the
-project case-study cover, and the project-card hover-distortion cover
-(rounds the WebGL canvas overlay along with the image underneath it,
-since they share one clipped container). Client and testimonial logos
-are left alone — they're marks, not photography.
-
-Updates the design-token comment and the styleguide's shape/radius
-copy (it/en/zh) to describe the new rule instead of the old
-"zero radius on media" one, so the documentation stays honest.
