-Subject: [PATCH] Load videos further ahead and stop tearing them down on a
- quick scroll-past
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Two things were compounding into visible jank while scrolling through a
-page of videos: the 300px activation margin didn't leave enough runway
-on a typical mobile connection for a video to actually finish buffering
-before it scrolled into view, so viewers watched it load; and a fast
-flick that carried a video briefly out of the margin and back tore its
-source down immediately, forcing a full reload from zero on the way
-back in.
-
-Widen the activation margin to 700px so buffering has more of a head
-start, and debounce the deactivate edge by a second so a quick pass
-doesn't discard an already-loading (or already-loaded) source. Entering
-the margin still activates immediately — only losing it is delayed.
